{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles","id":1505310,"title":"[For Fun] Splats as Spiritual/Xianxia Cultivation Methods/Scriptures/Styles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-14T05:33:49-07:00","id":1505310,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [For Fun] Splats as Spiritual/Xianxia Cultivation Methods/Scriptures/Styles","content":"Pretty much as the title says, if you were to turn one,or more, of the various CoD Splats into a Xianxia-esque Spiritual Cultivation Method/Scripture/Style, be it Canon (such as Changeling, Beast, Demon, Deviant, etc) or Homebrew (Genius, Leviathan, Princess, Siren, etc), what would it be? How would practitioners wield it, &amp; Initiates be inducted? What would the general disposition of those who utilised it be? What kind of Sects would they form? What resources would they utilise? And other such inquiries.<br /> <br /> Ya'll can discuss &amp; debate this all you like, I might even join in, but all I ask is that you obey the sites' rules of etiquette, &amp; that you at least <i>try</i> to stay on topic, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 03-17-2023, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T10:15:25-07:00","id":1505324,"title":"","content":"I'm going to advise against this conversation? Even if it's respectful towards religions, forms of spirituality, and metaphysical philosophies, there's probably just an inherent bad taste towards comparing them to stuff like this, particularly stuff like monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T18:29:52-07:00","id":1505400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1505324#post1505324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to advise against this conversation? Even if it's respectful towards religions, forms of spirituality, and metaphysical philosophies, there's probably just an inherent bad taste towards comparing them to stuff like this, particularly stuff like monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monstrosity is subjective. I don't know about Xianxia's tenets, but &quot;we cannot borrow aesthetics and tropes due to cultural sensitivity issues&quot; is a ship that sailed a VERY long time ago in both OWOD and ChroD. Seems like a defeatist attitude to me, especially considering that even monsters can have a moral compass as you yourself often talk about. Why can't a Mage have Xianxia as a magical style? What if he is descended from the original practitioners due to being part of a Proximus Dynasty, and this is just part of his people's mystical heritage?<br /> <br /> And even if he is not a biological descendant, stories about cultural and mystical exchange between Mages could be very interesting, and it's part of the Free Council's ethos as a pro-Sleeper, pro-democracy organization. There is such a thing as being under-informed and misrepresenting, but shooting down ideas on principle because someone out there might feel upset is not something I can get behind. What about the people who'd feel honored at a earnest attempt and would be willing to give an insider's perspective, are those people somehow wrong? Come on. Writing has always involved the risk of not being true to real life, but that's not reason to give up before even trying.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T18:49:26-07:00","id":1505401,"title":"","content":"Making a new post only to avoid the malfunctioning spam-detection bots.<br /> <br /> I guess a nebulously defined, highly personal &quot;inherent bad taste&quot; is enough of a pretext to discourage a civil, respectful and productive discussion between people approaching the topic in good faith and willing to learn new things that reaffirm their mutual humanity.<br /> <br /> But I'm a layman, don't mind me. We'll see how it works out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T18:57:04-07:00","id":1505403,"title":"","content":"And truth is...I've read a lot of Xianxia stories. Webnovels, but still.<br /> <br /> A straight port of morality from the Chronicles of Darkness would be <i>significantly more morally concerned </i>than a lot of genre fiction in Xianxia. They're <i>infamous </i>for having outright amoral protagonists where &quot;I am stronger than you&quot; is regarded as the only justification needed for really nasty behavior. Combine that with actual yaoguai and Demon Cultivators, along with Ghost Immortals, Heart Devils, Celestial Bureaucracy knows what else...there's plenty of monsters already in Xianxia that are already Mage-adjacent.<br /> <br /> So, I'll start. Keeping in mind I do not have the cultural background and have no idea if &quot;Niohuru Die&quot; is grammatically sensible:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: Way of Violent Harmony and Beast Cultivation</b><br /> <br /> It is a fact of life that many animals, if the order of the world glitches so that they become sentient, seek to become more human, and sometimes, they succeed. They are the yaoguai, kin to human cultivators - which was not lost on several schools. In particular, the Border Balancing Sect discovered that many humans are actually descendants of the lover of the Moon Goddess, Niohuru Die, a wolf yaoguai so old and wise he had practically become a god - and slain by his human descendants when they realized he had become stuck in his spiritual progression and was increasingly victimized by the Heart Devils who call themselves the Maeljin, a word that no one knows the origin of, all that it means profound wickedness and a desire for evolution at the cost of others and the world. To that effect, the Sect developed a way to call forth their forefather's inherited ki, allowing them to assume the form of wolf yaoguai and learn the world as only demons and other spirit beasts can, as something whose very consciousness is a violation of the will of Heaven. As an orthodox sect, the Border Balancers wish to maintain the harmony between the human and spirit worlds, but in sharp contrast to others, they do so through their bloodline talent with furious and aggressive fighting styles, to the point they are infamous for losing themselves in the midst of a hunt. To cultivators who seek to learn from them, however, beware their Heretical breakaway, the Pure Forest Rage School - to them, their capacity to assume both human and yaoguai forms mean they are something more akin to gods and spirits, and as atonement for their ancestors' lack of filial piety, wish to overwhelm the mortal kingdoms with legions of angry and vengeful spirits and rule over the wreckage. And <i>especially </i>beware the Maeljin, and the terrible Moon Nightmares who Niohuru once imprisoned in the house of his beloved, the spirits of the world before its ordering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T19:36:58-07:00","id":1505406,"title":"","content":"And then, a day later, I remember what xianxia actually is. Nvm the old argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T06:45:30-07:00","id":1512864,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire: blood</b><br /> <b>Mage: magic<br /> Geis: death</b><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T07:26:38-07:00","id":1512865,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Mandatory disclaimer:</b> Xianxia and Cultivation stories are based on ancient Chinese cosmologies and different mystical schools (Taoism mainly, but lots of Buddhist influence along folk religion and others), while being clearly a literary fantasy genre. The closest thing I can explain to gamers it would be the same way Dungeons and Dragons is based on (but not meant to be representative of) medieval stories and history.<br /> <br /> Since it copies from classical Chinese thinking, there are a lot of references to the <u>Heaven-Man-Earth</u> triad. <u>Heaven</u> is (usually) not the afterlife. When Cultivation/Xianxia says Heaven it could be several things: a higher plane of existence, the literal heavenly bodies or the spiritual part that all beings should have. <u>Earth</u> is the world itself, and the substance that beings are made of. And <u>Man</u> is literal mankind but also the rational parts that only humanity has among all Earthly beings.<br /> <br /> Depending on the variations, the afterlife could be a better version of your life on earth, reincarnation, dissolution in the great Dao, ghostly existence (related to the dual souls: Hun and P'o), or a combination of all of the above.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, based on <u>generic</u> stories:<ul><li>Regular cultivator techniques is <b>Mage</b>. The Arcana, Legacies and Prelacies, are the cultivation abilities, the Dao and the Heaven patronage respectively.\u200b</li> <li><b>Beast </b>and <b>Vampire </b>would be Demonic Cultivators, the Beast and the Horror could be thought as different types of Gu, spiritual contamination, demonic beings, etc.</li> <li>Spectral cultivators, <b>Geist </b>got you covered.</li> <li><b>Werewolves </b>and other shapeshifters would be Demonic Beasts (Be aware that Demons in Xianxia are usually two different categories: mutated animals/people OR spiritual entities; shapeshifters would be the first kind).</li> <li>The second type of demons are of course creatures from the lower depths: <b>Fiends </b>from Duat, <b>Demons </b>from Inferno, etc.</li> <li>All the <b>Ephemeral creatures</b> are Spiritual entities, some are nature-based (<b>Spirits</b>), Tulpas (<b>Goetia</b>), and Spectres (<b>Ghosts</b>), Heavenly beings are obviously God-Machine <b>Angels</b>, and Pure Heavenly beings are the <b>Supernal creatures</b>.</li> <li><b>Changelings </b>are a type of nature spirt and/or purified demonic beings.</li> <li><b>Prometheans</b>,<b> Deviants</b>, and <b>God Machine Demons</b> I have no idea where to put.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, <b>Mage the Awakening</b> (with a dash of <b>Second Sight</b>) is what better can represent typical Cultivation and Xianxia stories. Striving for the Heavens (starting with Archmastery and finally Ascension), Mana as Qi, Legacies as Dao, Scelestus / Infernalist as Demonic cultivators, the Heavenly tribulations when growing more powerful (Exarch intervention), all fit in the genre perfectly. The basic types of cultivators also get representation: martial (Arrow), academic (Mysterium), spies/assassins/manipulators (Guardians), royal/priestly (Ladder), independent thinkers (Free Council and Nameless Orders), and can still cover other types as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-30-2023, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T14:03:53-07:00","id":1512910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1512865#post1512865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]<b>Mandatory disclaimer:</b> Xianxia and Cultivation stories are based on ancient Chinese cosmologies and different mystical schools (Taoism mainly, but lots of Buddhist influence along folk religion and others), while being clearly a literary fantasy genre. The closest thing I can explain to gamers it would be the same way Dungeons and Dragons is based on (but not meant to be representative of) medieval stories and history.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>So having been in several cultivation and xianxia circles before I can tell you that while yeah they do use Taoism and Buddhist influence a majority of stories tend to dislike the Buddhist and Taoist section, more specifically the religion and not the influence. There are various reasons behind that, which would be a bit hard to explain but it's why a lot of the novels involving cultivation and Xianxia protagonists tend to be outright bastards as Leliel said. Mind there are good cultivation stuff that doesn't have the main character be amoral people and they are popular but a lot of people into this genre sorta assume that a protag is going to be amoral at best.<br /> <br /> In regards to cultivation in the chronicles of darkness, while its world of darkness hseifans <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/435620/Kindred-of-the-East-The-Relentless-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred of the East</a> remake is pretty much a cultivation game in the world of darkness.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:21:29-07:00","id":1513001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1512910#post1512910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>So having been in several cultivation and xianxia circles before I can tell you that while yeah they do use Taoism and Buddhist influence a majority of stories tend to dislike the Buddhist and Taoist section, more specifically the religion and not the influence.</b> There are various reasons behind that, which would be a bit hard to explain but it's why a lot of the novels involving cultivation and Xianxia protagonists tend to be outright bastards as Leliel said. Mind there are good cultivation stuff that doesn't have the main character be amoral people and they are popular but a lot of people into this genre sorta assume that a protag is going to be amoral at best.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? This aligns to what I wrote explaining that it was <i>based on</i> but does not <i>pretend to be</i> Taoism / Buddhism / etc... It has lots of things from them: reincarnation, otherworldly realms, constant meditation as a gateway to ascension, spiritual meridians, qi, etc.<br /> <br /> I did a very, very brief introduction to the genre, there are lots and lots of nuances (moral vs amoral protagonist, native vs isekai, traditional tropes vs novel takes on the genre, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1512910#post1512910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to cultivation in the chronicles of darkness, while its world of darkness hseifans <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/435620/Kindred-of-the-East-The-Relentless-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred of the East</a> remake is pretty much a cultivation game in the world of darkness.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I will review this too. Perhaps the OP will find something there that they like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T16:40:47-07:00","id":1513135,"title":"","content":"I was actually unaware that KotE was such, so I'll have to look into purchasing it once I've got the money to spare. \u2026Or just finding a free copy on the internet, either/or.<br /> <br /> Still, I certainly won't stop or discourage you from trying to fit the splats into the general shapes of Generic-style Xianxia, since I'm just trying to provide a prompt of some sort to act as a springboard from which to elaborate through your own creative prerogative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1512865#post1512865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Prometheans</b> and <b>God Machine Demons</b> I have no idea where to put.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Qi/Ki/Chi is often described as life energy or 'lifeforce', so maybe Prometheans could be the result of certain Alchemical events &amp; happenings causing such energy to be imbued into corpses of various sorts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T17:26:07-07:00","id":1513139,"title":"","content":"On Xianxia and the \u2018big\u2019 East Asian religions: Yeah, from what I observed, the former only takes \u2018background setting lore fluff\u2019 from the latter\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> On Promethean-xia: The Insatiate alchemists from the game pretty much <b>are</b> Xianxia-style cultivators in mindset.<br /> <br /> On Demon-xia: The GM as the oppressive rules of reality itself that deny cultivators their rightful godhood works as a background for Xianxia protagonists who at least pretend to be moral.<br /> Alternatively, we can stick with cultivators/the Unchained as assholes, and put the GM and its angels as the last line of cosmic decency.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Oops. The Relentless Age by hsienfan was already recommended above 05-28-2023, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T18:08:56-07:00","id":1513141,"title":"","content":"I had an outline of xianxia based Legacy some time ago, it would use Life and Prime. An Attainment would convert them into beings halfway between a platonic form and a living being. Mana would act as Qi and they would seek to cultivate by using internal alchemy to enhance themselves to be closer to their platonic ideal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T12:26:42-07:00","id":1513220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1513135#post1513135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually unaware that KotE was such, so I'll have to look into purchasing it once I've got the money to spare. \u2026Or just finding a free copy on the internet, either/or.<br /> <br /> Still, I certainly won't stop or discourage you from trying to fit the splats into the general shapes of Generic-style Xianxia, since I'm just trying to provide a prompt of some sort to act as a springboard from which to elaborate through your own creative prerogative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, Qi/Ki/Chi is often described as life energy or 'lifeforce', so maybe Prometheans could be the result of certain Alchemical events &amp; happenings causing such energy to be imbued into corpses of various sorts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fan made remake is the one you should be looking at to be specific, link should take you there and it's free.<br /> <br /> You don't need the old version of Kote","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T08:20:51-07:00","id":1513292,"title":"","content":"My experience with Xianxia is limited to a few unambitious Manhwas. Ones I ate up like the trash-eater I am. What they and this thread's suggestions have in common, is that they're optimistic and growth-oriented. Cultivators are seen to only ever rise upwards (or die). Here's where I say that Xianxia and Deviant could make for a dark and rich combination.<br /> <br /> Consider the old teachers. They encourage their students to advance the established methods, knowing that most of them will break their souls during experimentation. The masters wait until one of their subordinates discovers a rare, safe method of progress that they can then take for themselves. Until then, they help new recruits along to that breaking point, they make sure to maintain the veneer of superiority in front of their equals, they manage the volatile Remade who made a step into the unknown and suffered for it, and they look with jealous eyes at other masters.<br /> <br /> Who are those other masters? Manipulators who kept their souls intact. Remade, still buying into the lie. Patsies, built up to deflect suspicion from the real masterminds.<br /> <br /> Consider the students. Some are eager in their pursuit and trust in their seniors to steer them right. Some saw through the charade, but are confident that they will succeed where others failed. Some aim at becoming the new old teacher - safe from Divergence, but joining an elite few of paranoid, backstabbing liars. Some see through the system they're tangled in. They wish to retire with their few stable powers, but with their secret knowledge and their status as a possible guinea pigs, they're in straits as dire as any Remade.<br /> <br /> Consider the Remade themselves - Broken, but no weaker for it. Some that are certain in their superiority, competing for students, mystical resources, and jealously guarded methods. Some that realize the betrayal, and are faced with a machinery of desire that will always come back from destruction, as long as there is dangerous knowledge and people willing to use it. Both are a threat and and asset to the old teachers, to be manipulated and aimed at their opponents.<br /> <br /> Consider a World of Cultivation where the path to ascension in yet uncharted, where treacherous guides pretend to enlightenment, where your brothers and sisters in the art twist into monsters. Where Schools of Cultivation war with inhuman powers over hidden secrets and loud deceptions. Where ascension meets decay.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:38:52-07:00","id":1513335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1513292#post1513292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with Xianxia is limited to a few unambitious Manhwas. Ones I ate up like the trash-eater I am. What they and this thread's suggestions have in common, is that they're optimistic and growth-oriented. Cultivators are seen to only ever rise upwards (or die). Here's where I say that Xianxia and Deviant could make for a dark and rich combination.<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> Consider a World of Cultivation where the path to ascension in yet uncharted, where treacherous guides pretend to enlightenment, where your brothers and sisters in the art twist into monsters. Where Schools of Cultivation war with inhuman powers over hidden secrets and loud deceptions. Where ascension meets decay.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of most depictions of Ma-gong (calque \u201cdevil disciplines\u201d) in Korean webnovels/manhwa are usually depicted \u2014 quick path to power, even quicker path to mental degeneration and/or physical warping. (Sans protagonist exceptionalism, of course)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T01:05:40-07:00","id":1513364,"title":"","content":"The few Manhwas I read had this implied, but never taking center stage. Either way, this fits really well. I imagine that all the Schools are locked in a long-term propaganda game, where decrying another as Ma-gong is just another (hypocritical) tool in their arsenal. One to be used sparingly - if you condemn the arts of another, you can no longer justify using them yourself. Also, &quot;protagonist exceptionalism&quot; is exactly the attitude they want to see in their students. Many a Deviant would be a former wannabe MC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T01:53:49-07:00","id":1513366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1513364#post1513364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The few Manhwas I read had this implied, but never taking center stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s likely cuz the very first (non-web) Korean novel to have a Magyo-do (\u201cdevil-faith followe\u201d) protagonist had said protagonist at the peak of devil-mastery, the attainment of which enables the cultivator to flawlessly disguise and suppress the corruption\u2026 even on a psychospiritual level, so that he can have some semblance of moral reason. (Though he still has the Might Makes Right stuff) After this guy set the trope, the rest just followed suit.<br /> <br /> (Which makes following his particular example not so great for Deviant! This guy\u2019s more like a high-powered Aberrant or Abyssal Exalted)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, this fits really well. I imagine that all the Schools are locked in a long-term propaganda game, where decrying another as Ma-gong is just another (hypocritical) tool in their arsenal. One to be used sparingly - if you condemn the arts of another, you can no longer justify using them yourself. Also, &quot;protagonist exceptionalism&quot; is exactly the attitude they want to see in their students. Many a Deviant would be a former wannabe MC. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The masters will be pleased\u2026<br /> <br /> Hmm now I have another project to put on the backburner. Maybe something like the legendary Poison-Man of the Sichuan Dang clan or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T12:50:21-07:00","id":1518195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1513141#post1513141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an outline of xianxia based Legacy some time ago, it would use Life and Prime. An Attainment would convert them into beings halfway between a platonic form and a living being. Mana would act as Qi and they would seek to cultivate by using internal alchemy to enhance themselves to be closer to their platonic ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A bit of thread necromancy, but this just recently became relevant in my games.<br /> <br /> We went with a path to Archmastery striving to have fully Perfected Body, essentially perfected bones, flesh, blood, skin, etc as per Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T18:28:45-07:00","id":1518211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1518195#post1518195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A bit of thread necromancy, but this just recently became relevant in my games.<br /> <br /> We went with a path to Archmastery striving to have fully Perfected Body, essentially perfected bones, flesh, blood, skin, etc as per Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one spell that might be interesting is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1413312#post1413312\">Create Immortal Jade</a>. The idea of the Legacy was inspired by the cultivation paths in <i>I Shall Seal the Heavens</i>, which means it would look terrifying to most modern people. Each level would mean gaining one transcendent step, like higher awareness at the start (<i>True Sight</i> to see all layers of Twilight), the ability to purge diseases, maybe some level of alchemical creations ex nihilo using platonic forms, unfortunately I only have a rough outline at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T08:37:47-07:00","id":1518245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1505310-for-fun-splats-as-spiritual-xianxia-cultivation-methods-scriptures-styles?p=1518211#post1518211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, one spell that might be interesting is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1413312#post1413312\">Create Immortal Jade</a>. The idea of the Legacy was inspired by the cultivation paths in <i>I Shall Seal the Heavens</i>, which means it would look terrifying to most modern people. Each level would mean gaining one transcendent step, like higher awareness at the start (<i>True Sight</i> to see all layers of Twilight), the ability to purge diseases, maybe some level of alchemical creations ex nihilo using platonic forms, unfortunately I only have a rough outline at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liked the spell, in our case the path is to have an effect that is a Lasting Life version of &quot;Hone the Perfected Form&quot; either as part of a Legacy, or most likely as one of the Life Archmastery paths to attain true immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T13:03:13-07:00","id":1550914,"title":"","content":"Bumpa-bumpa boing-boing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T05:25:29-07:00","id":1550937,"title":"","content":"Promethean!<br /> <br /> Let's compare Prometheans to spirit beasts. They both undergo alchemical transformations, gaining more understanding and power, all on the way towards an improved state of being. They intuit information they shouldn't have access to, be it through Azothic Memory or the Dao. On their path, they face Firestorms and Heavenly Tribulations, all the time being threatened by Alchemists and Cultivators wanting to exploit their bodies for their own benefit. Now, their end-state could be considerably different, but other than that, you could switch them around between their respective settings and still have both genres work. In fact, you could draft a Chinese Dark Era with both Prometheans and spirit beasts being tied through Divine fire, striving to attain humanity and maybe... <i>maybe</i> move beyond it. The biggest challenge would be to reconcile their differing themes. A fictional world could criticize Xianxia's disrespect towards baseline human experience, but also deconstruct Promethean's rejection of trans-humanism, and create a harmonious whole.<br /> <br /> Mummy!<br /> <br /> The Heavens would have a much different flavor to them, if they're replaced by Duat. It is as if Heavens and Hell were combined into a new institution. Something more hands-on, legalistic, righteous, insane and cruel. At first, it would be easier to grow in power by working <i>with</i> Duat, rather than challenging it - as a member of a Cult. At least until a member desires more than they can get, which leads to their sudden but inevitable betrayal. Some Judges would be inclined to open paths of Cultivation (like Nekhenku or Arem-Abfu), but also punish following them wrong (Arem-Abfu), or even embarking upon them (Usekh-Nemtet). Sorcery, intricate but mysterious metaphysics and soul-surgery are already part of the setting, just with Egyptian, rather than east-Asian flair. Consider Cultivators debating intricacies of five Pillars rather than Wuxing, and figuring out which mention of Chi refers to Ka, specifically, and which to Sekhem as a whole. You can get an eclectic fusion of the two cultures, like the Four Guardian Beasts being used as protectors of canopic jars, or Ox-Head and Horse-Head fighting with Fiends over who gets to guard Duat's gates. Also, Immortals are a valid type of PC/NPC in Mummy, and advanced Cultivators could join that &quot;elite&quot;, looking down smugly on Blood-Bathers and Body-Snatchers they rub shoulders with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T14:03:58-07:00","id":1551244,"title":"","content":"I love many of these ideas.<br /> <br /> My personal pick: Humans and Hunters!<br /> No, seriously. If I wanted Xianxia concepts with a ChroD Game, and not make a new Splat or minor Template, I'd go with Humans/Hunters (that, or Prometheans due to the already mentioned focus on philosophical understanding and insight, e.g. as Teatime mentioned above). I'd stack up on the martial fighting styles for fluff, and mecanically change compacts and conspiracies to sects and clans, and would change who can access which etc., but many concepts are already there and only need some fluffing/ tweaking like making fighting style and fighting merits half price or something like that, to have more of them thrown around (also, with Martial Arts 5 Touch of Death, Brute Force 1 Falling Pillar and Relentless Assault 2 Eye of the Tiger. you can use All-out attacks at no loss of Defense against a single target, dealing 2L damage with bare hands and 8-again - all for 8/4 xp).<br /> One reason is that humans and hunters are the ones that most capture the &quot;starting out&quot; feeling of these types of novels and manhua, and I personally usually prefer the first few arcs over the middle or endgame. More tension, more potential for growth, less overload of pseudophilosophical Dao-babble bullshido (&quot;His blade is so powerful because it captures the essence of sharpness but withholds the cut!!!11eleven&quot; - don't get me wrong, some do this well, abd I love it when they do, but then, the words <i>mean </i>something.) etc.<br /> But specifically, groups like Ascending Ones (slightly tweaked for this; Orthodox/'Righteous') and Cheiron (Unorthodox) already hunt down Monsters to protect people/to use parts of them to empower themselves to hunt down more to get more parts to hunt down more... like cultivators and spirit beasts /spirit beast tides. Ascending Ones then would be one of the few rare righteous sects where Cultivators actually care about people and use the monster parts in their alchemy Elixiers, while Cheiron are heretical monster bloodline cultivators with very unorthodox but effective body tempering and grafting procedures.<br /> Hunt Club and Bear Lodge already fit the 'just wanna fight the strong, it's fun' mold. Throw in some Cainite Heresy Hunters are already tainted with dark powers they use for good (or keep them seperate as a tragic demonic-blooded but otherwise orthodox clan that uses their evil blood magics for good).<br /> Just fudge a few things around, and you have the trappings of a sect of an unorthodox sect that uses a forbidden form of body tempering and blood magics to rise and fight - to borrow from Murim manwha, a Divine Demon/Blood Cult type of sect.<br /> With this, you can play up the 'ancient cultivators fighting demonic beasts and have sect wars' angle, or go for the modern variety.<br /> <br /> As the game goes on, I'd have them slowly turn into a Splat as a major breakthrough, 'fortuitous encounter' or specific cultivation method (&quot;Drinking Blood is part of our cultivation art; we circulate the blood Qi; Side effects are being susceptible to all forms of Yin energy, so keep out of the sun&quot;, &quot;This Cultivation Technique replaces parts of your souls with a Ghost/Spirit; here's how you circulate from now on: you punch people when they are down, literally and metaphorically&quot;), usually at the Realm at which one would be considered a &quot;intermediate Realm cultivator&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-23-2025, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}